From d7cbfd1a4744335ac950ba24b2002852058f2b0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VERHILLE Arnaud <gist974@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:10:16 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/19] 68020 core: the discarded refill is an instruction
 fetch without a cache too

readStatusRefill() sent the discarded program word through readInstr() only
when the instruction cache is emulated. Without one, it used a plain program
read, which skips what readInstr() charges every other instruction word
fetched from a port narrower than 32 bits (dsack()).

The refill now goes through readInstr() on every 68020-core model, so the
discarded word costs what any other fetched word costs on that bus. An
instruction prefetch is one bus cycle on a 32-bit port and two on a 16-bit
port (MC68020UM Table 5-6, MC68030UM Table 7-6).

The timing tables show a second prefetch for MOVE EA,SR, 11(0/2/0) worst
case (MC68020UM 8.2.7), and three for an expired DBcc, 10(0/3/0) (8.2.15).
They show none for MOVE EA,CCR, 5(0/1/0), nor for a trapping TRAPV, which
has the prefetches of TRAP #n (8.2.17): the discarded read of those two is
Moira's model, and this change only makes it cost what the model's other
fetches cost. MC68030UM 12.7.1 ties the refill to operations that can
change the program space.

The change reaches the models whose instruction cache is not emulated: the
68040 family, and a 68020 or 68030 built with MOIRA_EMULATE_ICACHE=false.
The expired DBcc and the trapping TRAPV are concerned only once they go
through readStatusRefill(). The charge follows the host's dsack() answer,
and with the default 16-bit answer a 68040 pays it although MC68040UM 7.2
says the 68040 does not size its bus dynamically: a host that models a
68040 bus answers DSACK_32, and then nothing changes.
---
 Moira/MoiraDataflow_cpp.h | 6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Moira/MoiraDataflow_cpp.h b/Moira/MoiraDataflow_cpp.h
index dd92749..2cf66f1 100644
--- a/Moira/MoiraDataflow_cpp.h
+++ b/Moira/MoiraDataflow_cpp.h
@@ -870,10 +870,8 @@ Moira::readStatusRefill()
 {
     u32 addr = C == Core::C68000 ? reg.pc : reg.pc + 2;
     if constexpr (C == Core::C68020) {
-        if (iCache.emulated) {
-            (void)readInstr<C>(addr);
-            return;
-        }
+        (void)readInstr<C>(addr);
+        return;
     }
     (void)read<C, AddrSpace::PROG, Word>(addr);
 }
